0..67 Comment "// The refusals of implicit parameters: a call omitting an implicit"
68..135 Comment "// nothing determines, one whose only solution names a binder of an"
136..213 Comment "// argument\'s own lambda, a call whose argument and expected type disagree on"
214..282 Comment "// one, an implicit written among the parentheses, a resident naming"
283..355 Comment "// no implicit, a use standing as a value with an implicit unsupplied, a"
356..431 Comment "// supply standing as a value whose implicit, once the supply abstracts the"
432..500 Comment "// explicit parameter before it, holds no value of that parameter, a"
501..577 Comment "// telescope whose types mention each other, and a positional supply after a"
578..656 Comment "// named one, past the block, twice, or compound. A call in a declared type is"
657..731 Comment "// refused as one in a body is: the type\'s formation solves its implicits."
732..734 Comment "//"
735..749 Comment "// - see: #315"
750..765 Comment "// - see: #1216"
766..823 Comment "// - see: #5026 — `unchosenSigned`, `disagreeingSigned`"
825..903 Comment "// `same`, the identity at a type supplied by name, `twice`, whose combination"
904..981 Comment "// is implicit, `chosen`, whose implicit\'s type names its explicit parameter,"
982..1057 Comment "// and `konst`, whose implicit is the result type of the function it takes."
